---
id: org.dxos.plugin.meetingRecorder
name: MeetingRecorderPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Granola-style meeting notes for calls held in other apps. On Composer Desktop the plugin notices when
another app (Zoom, Meet in a browser, Teams, FaceTime, Slack, …) starts using the microphone, offers
to take notes, and records the call into a `Meeting` (plugin-meeting) with a live transcript — the
microphone as the local user, the system audio as the other participants. When the app releases the
microphone the recording stops and the meeting is summarized.

The native half is the `tauri-plugin-meeting-capture` crate
(`packages/apps/composer-app/src-tauri/plugins/meeting-capture`), modelled on anarlog's `detect` and
`audio` crates: CoreAudio process objects (`kAudioProcessPropertyIsRunningInput`) for detection and a
global process tap for system audio. A browser build records the microphone only, started by hand.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`       |

## Types

```mdl
type MicApp
  desc: An app holding the microphone, as the native side reports it.
  fields:
    id: string                        # bundle id (us.zoom.xos), or pid:<n>
    name: string                      # display name
```

```mdl
type RecorderState
  desc: The recorder's lifecycle; held in MeetingRecorderCapabilities.State.
  literals: idle | detected | starting | recording | stopping
  fields:
    app?: MicApp                      # detected / starting / recording
    meeting?: Meeting                 # recording / stopping
    startedAt?: number                # recording; epoch ms
    systemAudio?: boolean             # recording; other participants are transcribed too
```

```mdl
type Settings
  fields:
    detectMeetings: boolean           # default true; desktop only
    autoStart: boolean                # default false; record without asking
    autoStop: boolean                 # default true; stop when the app releases the mic
    autoSummarize: boolean            # default true; MeetingOperation.Summarize on stop
    captureSystemAudio: boolean       # default true; desktop only
    ignoredApps?: string[]            # bundle ids; defaults to dictation, IDE, screen-recorder apps
```

## Components

```mdl
component RecorderStatus
  desc: Status-bar item standing in for Granola's menu-bar control.
  state:
    phase: RecorderState
  actions:
    record() → void                   # idle: op:Start
    takeNotes() → void                # detected: op:Start { app }
    dismiss() → void                  # detected: op:ClearDetection
    stop() → void                     # recording: op:Stop
  layout: |
    idle       [●]
    detected   [● Take notes · Zoom] [×]
    recording  [■ Recording 2:13 · Zoom]
```

## Operations

```mdl
op Start
  key: org.dxos.operation.meetingRecorder.start
  desc: Creates a Meeting in the given (or active) space, opens it, and starts transcribing the microphone and, on desktop, the system audio.
  input:
    name?: string                     # default "<App> meeting · <date>"
    app?: MicApp
    db?: Database                     # default: active space, else the default space
  output:
    object: Meeting
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [MeetingRecorderCapabilities.Recorder, TranscriptionCapabilities.TranscriptionManagerProvider]
  note: Idempotent while recording — returns the meeting already being recorded.
```

```mdl
op Stop
  key: org.dxos.operation.meetingRecorder.stop
  desc: Stops capture after the buffered audio is transcribed, then summarizes the meeting when autoSummarize is on.
  input: {}
  output: void
  effects: [ai:inference]
```

```mdl
op HandleDetection
  key: org.dxos.operation.meetingRecorder.handleDetection
  desc: Applies the settings and ignore list to a change in the apps using the microphone; prompts, starts or stops accordingly.
  input:
    type: micStarted | micStopped
    apps: MicApp[]
  output: void
  note: Invoked by the native detection listener for every change; invocable directly where the host cannot observe other apps.
```

```mdl
op ClearDetection
  key: org.dxos.operation.meetingRecorder.clearDetection
  desc: Returns a detected-but-unanswered meeting to idle without recording it.
  input: {}
  output: void
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Meeting Detection

  req F-1.1: On desktop, the native side reports every change in the set of apps holding the microphone, excluding Composer and the WebKit helpers that record on its behalf.
  req F-1.2:
    when: a non-ignored app starts using the microphone and the recorder is idle
    then: the recorder enters `detected` and shows a "Take notes" prompt naming the app
  req F-1.3: Apps in the ignore list (dictation, IDEs, screen recorders, AI assistants) never prompt.
  req F-1.4: With autoStart, detection starts recording without a prompt.
  req F-1.5: A detected app releasing the microphone before the prompt is answered returns the recorder to idle.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Recording

  req F-2.1: Starting creates a Meeting (with transcript, notes and summary) in the active space and opens it.
  req F-2.2: The microphone is transcribed with the local identity as sender.
  req F-2.3: On desktop, the system audio is transcribed with sender "<App> participants".
  req F-2.4: Each source is segmented at speech pauses (SpeakingMonitor), not at a fixed interval.
  req F-2.5: Without system-audio permission the recording continues from the microphone alone.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Stopping

  req F-3.1: Stopping transcribes the audio still buffered before closing the pipeline.
  req F-3.2: With autoStop, the meeting app releasing the microphone stops the recording.
  req F-3.3: With autoSummarize, stopping runs MeetingOperation.Summarize on the meeting.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Detect, prompt and record
  given: the recorder is idle and detectMeetings is on
  when: op:HandleDetection { type: micStarted, apps: [{ id: us.zoom.xos, name: zoom.us }] }, then the prompt's "Take notes"
  then:
    - state passes through detected → starting → recording with app.id === us.zoom.xos
    - a Meeting named "Zoom meeting · <date>" exists in the active space and is open
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Ignored app
  given: the recorder is idle
  when: op:HandleDetection { type: micStarted, apps: [{ id: com.superduper.superwhisper, name: superwhisper }] }
  then: state stays idle and no prompt is shown
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Meeting ends
  given: the recorder is recording a meeting detected in app A, autoStop on
  when: op:HandleDetection { type: micStopped, apps: [A] }
  then:
    - state returns to idle after the buffered audio is transcribed
    - with autoSummarize, meeting.summary becomes non-empty
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Detect a meeting in another app and record it into a Meeting
  desc: The Granola round-trip — a meeting app takes the microphone, the user takes notes, speech is transcribed, the meeting ends and is summarized.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.2, F-1.5, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.4, F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.3, T-1, T-3]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-meeting and plugin-meeting-recorder are enabled
    - microphone permission is granted; speech reaches the microphone (in automation, Chromium's
      `--use-file-for-fake-audio-capture` playing a recorded voice file)
    - the EDGE transcription endpoint (`<edge>/calls/transcribe`) is reachable
  steps:
    - name: A meeting app takes the microphone
      do: Join a Zoom call (on desktop the native listener reports it on its own).
      invoke: [op:HandleDetection] { type: "micStarted", apps: [{ id: "us.zoom.xos", name: "zoom.us" }] }
      expect: a "Zoom meeting detected" prompt appears and the status bar shows "Take notes · Zoom"
      note: In a browser the host cannot observe other apps, so the event is invoked directly — the same operation the native listener calls.
    - name: Take notes
      do: Click "Take notes" in the prompt or the status bar.
      expect: a Meeting named "Zoom meeting · <date>" opens and the status bar shows a running "Recording" timer
    - name: Write a note while the meeting runs
      do: Type a line into the meeting's Notes tab.
      expect: the note is saved in meeting.notes
    - name: Speak
      do: Talk for a few sentences, pausing between them.
      expect: each utterance appears as a message in the Transcript tab within a few seconds of the pause
    - name: The meeting ends
      do: Leave the Zoom call.
      invoke: [op:HandleDetection] { type: "micStopped", apps: [{ id: "us.zoom.xos", name: "zoom.us" }] }
      expect: the status bar returns to the record button and a "Meeting saved" toast appears
    - name: Read the summary
      do: Open the meeting's Summary tab.
      expect: an AI summary of the transcript and the note appears
      note: Calls a live model; non-deterministic and needs the AI service.
  after:
    - name: Delete the meeting
      do: Right-click the meeting in the navtree and choose Delete.
      expect: the meeting leaves the navtree
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap            # named input parameters
    output?: TypeExpr           # return type
    errors?: ErrorMap           # name: Prose  (when this error occurs)
    effects?: EffectList        # echo:read | echo:write | http | fs | ai:inference | calls:activity
    requires?: ServiceList      # injected service dependencies
    note?: Prose                # implementation guidance (non-normative)
```
